(Compile-fail regression: a mutual cycle assembled across a `see`, where each
 file is internally legal. This file's `hoop` holds a `ring`; the seen file's
 `ring` holds a `hoop`. Neither parser could see the other half while every
 rule was enforced per file, so the analyzer's registry walk was the only
 thing standing between this and a layout of infinite size.

 The parse reads the seen file into the same identifier space now, so it is
 refused earlier and more plainly: the seen file's `ring` is the second
 definition of a name this file already claimed. Either way the program must
 not compile, and that is what this pins.)

A thing called ring has
  a number called radius is 0.

see "./include/hoop_holding_a_ring.vox".

A thing called hoop has
  a ring called band,
  a number called width is 0.

a hoop called wheel.
Print wheel's width.
